unit PascalCommon.HttpClientTests;

{ Loopback tests for PcNewHttpTransport (PascalCommon.Http.Client) against a
  server in this process, over plain TCP and over TLS with the certificates
  of tests/pki (docs/http-design.md, H10). No Docker server.

  The server runs one thread per connection (the probe's one-at-a-time
  servers distorted two Delphi numbers, finding 13) and answers by the
  request's path: a normal answer, an echo of what was sent, chunked with
  trailers, framed by the close, 1xx before the answer, duplicate headers, a
  302, and the broken ones (a line that isn't HTTP, a close before the
  status line, a truncated body, a bad chunk size, a folded header, a
  transfer coding other than chunked, oversized head and body, a body that
  isn't UTF-8, silence). It counts
  connections, so the pool's tests check reuse from the server's side.

  THttpClientTests runs over plain TCP. THttpsClientTests runs the TLS cases
  with the client and the server on the same backend: tbDefault, and on
  Windows a subclass on OpenSSL (it prints why and passes when OpenSSL can't
  be loaded, as PascalCommon.TlsTransportTests does).

  DUnitX master. The FPCUnit mirror (tests/Unit/fpc) is generated by
  tools/gen_fpc_mirror.py; never edit the mirror by hand. }

interface

